# Content Locales (i18n)

## Canonical shape

Everything downstream of `i18nResolve` (RenderPage, inspector) consumes
ONE shape, regardless of how the host stores it:

```
i18nProps: {
  en: { title: "Hello", desc: "…" },
  ne: { title: "नमस्ते", desc: "…" },
}
```

## Accepted input strategies (all must normalize to the shape above)

- **A — Nested** (`i18nProps.en.desc`) — default, preferred.
- **B — Flat suffix keys** (`desc_en` / `desc_ne`, or host aliases like
  `desp_eng` / `desp_np`) — mapped to locale codes via HOST CONFIG
  (`flatSuffixes` on each locale entry), never hardcoded in engine code.
- **C — Shared value** (`props.desc` only, declared in `sharedProps`) — one
  value for all locales, not duplicated per locale.

## Hard rules

- Never write `if (lang === 'ne') props.desp_np` or any similar per-locale
  branch inside a block's `render`. All locale resolution happens in
  `i18nResolve` before `render` ever sees props.
- Missing locale value → `fallbackLocale`. An empty string is a valid,
  intentional value and is NOT the same as missing — don't conflate them.
- Locale list, `defaultLocale`, `fallbackLocale`, and `localeStorage`
  (`'nested' | 'flat'`) all come from host config
  (`locales: [{ code, label, dir, flatSuffixes }]`). Do not hardcode `en`/
  `ne` as the only supported locales anywhere in engine code — the host
  may add `hi`, `zh`, etc. without an engine release.
- Inspector always edits the LOGICAL key (e.g. `desc`) for the currently
  active locale — never a flat key directly.
- Switching active locale changes which `i18nProps` slice is shown; it
  never duplicates or restructures the block tree.
- Copy/paste and duplicate must preserve the FULL `i18nProps` map (all
  locales), not just the active one.
- Rich text in any locale still passes through `sanitizeRichText` — full
  Unicode (Nepali/Devanagari) must survive sanitization; only active
  script content (script tags, event handlers) gets stripped.
- `dir` / `lang` attributes on the rendered page root follow the active
  locale.

## Performance note

Only the active locale's inputs should mount in the inspector at once
(don't render N locale tab panels simultaneously for pages with many
configured locales) — but ALL locales remain present in the underlying
data regardless of which tab is open.
